english_question:
A square ABCD with a side length of 1 is folded along the diagonal BD, connecting AC to form the triangular pyramid C-ABD. Its front view and top view are congruent isosceles right triangles, as shown in the figure. What is the area of the side view? ( )
A. \frac { 1 } { 4 }
B. \frac { 1 } { 2 }
C. \frac { \sqrt { 2 } } { 2 }
D. 1

The three views of a geometric body are shown in the figure, where the front view is an equilateral triangle. What is the volume of this geometric body?
A. 1
B. \frac { \sqrt { 3 } } { 3 }
C. \sqrt { 3 }
D. \frac { 2 \sqrt { 3 } } { 3 }

In the figure, the edge length of the cube ABCD-A₁B₁C₁D₁ is 1. P is the midpoint of BC, and Q is the midpoint of segment CC₁. What is the sum of the areas of the front view, side view, and top view of tetrahedron A₁PQD? ( )
A. \frac{5}{4}
B. 2
C. \frac{9}{4}
D. \frac{5}{2}

The three views of a certain geometric body are shown in the figure. What is the volume of this geometric body?
A. 6
B. 2 \sqrt{3}
C. 3
D. 3 \sqrt{3}
